## Security Baseline Review

Several Windows security configuration areas were reviewed before creating the controlled vulnerability.

### Windows Firewall

Firewall profile status was reviewed using:

```powershell
Get-NetFirewallProfile | Select-Object Name,Enabled
```

---

### SMBv1

SMBv1 status was reviewed using:

```powershell
Get-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName SMB1Protocol
```

SMBv1 was not enabled for testing.

---

### Guest Account

Guest-account status was reviewed using:

```powershell
Get-LocalUser Guest | Select-Object Name,Enabled
```

---

### Local Administrators

Local administrative membership was reviewed using:

```powershell
Get-LocalGroupMember Administrators
```

No accounts were removed as part of the assessment.

---

### Microsoft Defender

Defender status was reviewed using:

```powershell
Get-MpComputerStatus | Select-Object AntivirusEnabled,RealTimeProtectionEnabled
```

---

### Windows Updates

Recent hotfixes were reviewed using:

```powershell
Get-HotFix | Sort-Object InstalledOn -Descending | Select-Object -First 10 HotFixID,InstalledOn
```

This was treated as a recent-update inventory and not as a complete vulnerability scan.

---

### Remote Desktop

RDP configuration was reviewed using:

```powershell
Get-ItemProperty 'HKLM:\System\CurrentControlSet\Control\Terminal Server' | Select-Object fDenyTSConnections
```

