## MITRE ATT&CK Context

Relevant ATT&CK context:

```text
T1135 — Network Share Discovery
```

The vulnerability itself does not prove that Network Share Discovery occurred.

Instead:

```text
VULN-001 could increase exposure to network-share discovery and
subsequent unauthorized share access.
```

---

## Remediation Plan

Because the share existed only for controlled testing, the selected remediation was:

```text
Remove the unnecessary SMB share.
```

A production alternative could include restricting share access to an approved security group.

---

## Remediation

The vulnerable share was removed using:

```powershell
Remove-SmbShare -Name VULN31TEST -Force
```

Local verification confirmed the share no longer existed.

```powershell
Get-SmbShare -Name VULN31TEST
```

returned no valid share.

---

## Remote Remediation Verification

WIN11-01 was used to retest remote access.

```cmd
dir \\WIN11-02\VULN31TEST
```

Remote access failed after remediation.

A second read attempt:

```cmd
type \\WIN11-02\VULN31TEST\test.txt
```

also failed.

This confirmed that the vulnerable exposure was removed.

---

## Cleanup

The local test directory was removed:

```powershell
Remove-Item C:\VULN31TEST -Recurse -Force
```

Cleanup was verified using:

```powershell
Test-Path C:\VULN31TEST
```

Expected:

```text
False
```

